    "data": "Two phase II interventional trials are recruiting KRAS G12C‑mutated non‑small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) patients. NCT07670013 (Second Affiliated Hospital, Zhejiang University) evaluates SKB264 (4 mg/kg q2w) plus Glecirasib (600 mg QD) as first‑line therapy in an estimated 43 patients, using a Simon two‑stage design. Primary endpoint is objective response rate (ORR) per RECIST 1.1; secondary endpoints include disease control rate, duration of response, time to response, progression‑free survival, overall survival, and safety per NCI‑CTCAE 5.0. NCT07164170 (Abbisko Therapeutics) enrolls up to 86 patients in a single‑group, open‑label study of ABSK043 combined with Glecirasib in a 21‑day cycle, with an escalation (≈50 patients) and expansion (≈36 treatment‑naïve) part. Primary outcomes are dose‑limiting toxicities, adverse events, serious adverse events, and ORR; secondary outcomes cover pharmacokinetics, DOR, PFS, DCR, TTP, and OS. Both trials exclude prior KRAS G12C inhibitors, TROP2‑ADC, and other targetable driver mutations (EGFR, ALK, ROS1, RET, NTRK, BRAF V600E, MET exon 14). PD‑L1 positivity (≥1%) is required for certain cohorts. The studies aim to establish efficacy and safety of these novel KRAS G12C‑targeted combinations.",
